---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/global/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import HeroText from '../components/hero/HeroText.astro';
import SplitFeature from '../components/sections/SplitFeature.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/sections/CtaBand.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About WW Roofing & Building | Leeds"
  description="WW Roofing & Building is a roofing and building contractor based in Crossgates, east Leeds, working on houses, commercial buildings and construction projects across the city."
>
  <HeroText
    kicker="About WW"
    heading="A roofing and building firm from east Leeds"
    lede="WW Roofing & Building works from Crossgates, across Leeds and the towns around it. Roofing is the core of the business; building work grew out of doing the roof right and being asked what else we could take on."
  />

  <div class="wrap" style="padding-block-start: var(--space-4)">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
  </div>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>
        Every job starts with looking properly. Roofs get condemned every day that need
        three hours of repair, and roofs get patched every day that need replacing; the
        difference is somebody bothering to look and being straight about what they see.
        That is the reputation we are interested in.
      </p>
      <p>
        Quotes are written, itemised and explained. Sites are kept tidy because a tidy
        scaffold is a safe one and because it is your home or your business underneath
        it. And the parts of the job that get covered up, the membrane, the battens, the
        leadwork, get photographed as we go, so you can see what you paid for.
      </p>
      <h2>What we stand behind</h2>
      <p>
        The work on this site is our own, photographed by the people who did it. We
        would rather show you a roof half-finished, with the setting-out lines still
        visible, than a stock photograph of someone else's finished one. If you want to
        judge us, judge us on <a href="/projects/">the work</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Who you will deal with</h2>
      <p>
        The people who quote your job are the people who run it. Questions get answered
        by someone who has stood on your roof, not a call centre. It is a simple way to
        work and it is the reason most of our jobs arrive by word of mouth.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SplitFeature
    kicker="The evidence"
    heading="Judge us on the work"
    photoSlug="stone-slate-reslate-half-laid"
    photoVariant="clean"
    mediaSide="right"
    ctaHref="/projects/"
    ctaLabel="Browse our work"
    photoCaption="Heritage slope part way through re-slating"
  >
    <p>
      From full re-roofs on family homes to reclaimed stone slate on heritage
      buildings, the projects archive shows how we leave a roof, and just as
      importantly, what it looked like half way through.
    </p>
  </SplitFeature>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>
